---
import Layout from '../components/Layout.astro';
import { loadSiteData } from '../lib/data';
import { DISCLAIMER, REPO_URL, SITE_NAME, formatDate, formatDateTime } from '../lib/constants';
import { withBase } from '../lib/url';

const site = loadSiteData();
const articleCount = Object.keys(site.articles).length;
const cardCount = site.front.reduce((total, container) => total + container.cards.length, 0);
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description={DISCLAIMER}
	pillar="news"
>
	<article class="about">
		<header class="about__header">
			<p class="about__kicker">About</p>
			<h1 class="about__headline">What {SITE_NAME} is</h1>
			<p class="about__standfirst">
				{SITE_NAME} takes the Guardian&rsquo;s front page and asks a language model to rewrite each story in a
				more constructive register. The facts stay put; only the framing moves.
			</p>
		</header>

		<div class="about__body">
			<h2>An experiment, not a news service</h2>
			<p>
				This site is an AI-rewriting experiment. Every headline, standfirst and article body you see here was
				generated by a language model from a Guardian article, then published unedited. It is not journalism,
				it is not a correction of anyone&rsquo;s reporting, and it should not be read as a source of record.
				For the reporting itself, follow the source link at the foot of any story.
			</p>

			<h2>Not affiliated with Guardian News &amp; Media</h2>
			<p>
				{SITE_NAME} has no connection to Guardian News &amp; Media, is not endorsed by them, and does not
				speak for them. The Guardian&rsquo;s name appears here only to credit the source of each story.
				Bylines on this site are pseudonyms; the original author is always named and linked in the article
				footer.
			</p>

			<h2>Facts unchanged, framing changed</h2>
			<p>
				The rewrite brief is narrow: keep every verifiable claim, every name, number, date and quotation
				exactly as published, and change only the emphasis and tone. A fact-checking pass compares each
				rewrite against its source. When a rewrite fails that check, or the rewrite was skipped, the story is
				published as headline-only with a notice saying so and a link to the original.
			</p>

			<h2>What leads, and why</h2>
			<p>
				{SITE_NAME} carries the same stories as the Guardian&rsquo;s front page, but not always in the same
				order. Each story is scored on how much genuine progress its own reporting describes, and the strongest
				lead each section. &ldquo;What&rsquo;s going right&rdquo; gathers recent Guardian stories that are good
				news in their own right. The &ldquo;What&rsquo;s being done&rdquo; line at the top of a story names who is acting on
				it, drawn only from the original reporting. Stories too bleak to reframe honestly are left out rather
				than spun.
			</p>

			<h2>How it is built</h2>
			<p>
				A scheduled job reads the Guardian front page, sends each article through the rewrite engine, checks
				the result and assembles a single JSON file. This site is a static build over that one file &mdash;
				no database, no server, and no client-side JavaScript. The code is at{' '}
				<a href={REPO_URL} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">the source repository</a>.
			</p>

			<p class="about__disclaimer">{DISCLAIMER}</p>
		</div>

		<section class="status" aria-labelledby="status-title">
			<h2 class="status__title" id="status-title">Data status</h2>
			<dl class="status__list">
				<div class="status__row">
					<dt>Edition</dt>
					<dd>
						<time datetime={site.date}>{formatDate(site.date)}</time>
					</dd>
				</div>
				<div class="status__row">
					<dt>Generated at</dt>
					<dd>
						<time datetime={site.generatedAt}>{formatDateTime(site.generatedAt)}</time>
					</dd>
				</div>
				<div class="status__row">
					<dt>Rewrite engine</dt>
					<dd>{site.engine}</dd>
				</div>
				<div class="status__row">
					<dt>Front page cards</dt>
					<dd>{cardCount} across {site.front.length} containers</dd>
				</div>
				<div class="status__row">
					<dt>Full articles</dt>
					<dd>{articleCount}</dd>
				</div>
			</dl>
			<p class="status__note">
				<a class="status__link" href={withBase('/')}>Back to the front page</a>
			</p>
		</section>
	</article>
</Layout>

<style>
	.about {
		padding-top: var(--space-4);
		padding-bottom: var(--space-10);
	}

	.about__kicker {
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: var(--size-sans-14);
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--pillar);
		margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
	}

	.about__headline {
		font-family: var(--font-headline);
		font-weight: 700;
		font-size: var(--size-headline-34);
		line-height: var(--leading-headline);
		max-width: 46rem;
	}

	.about__standfirst {
		font-family: var(--font-body);
		font-size: var(--size-sans-20);
		line-height: 1.35;
		font-weight: 600;
		color: var(--neutral-20);
		max-width: var(--measure);
		margin-top: var(--space-4);
	}

	@media (min-width: 740px) {
		.about__headline {
			font-size: var(--size-headline-40);
		}
	}

	.about__body {
		max-width: var(--measure);
		padding-top: var(--space-5);
		font-family: var(--font-body);
		font-size: var(--size-body-17);
		line-height: var(--leading-body);
	}

	.about__body h2 {
		font-family: var(--font-headline);
		font-size: var(--size-headline-20);
		font-weight: 700;
		margin: var(--space-6) 0 var(--space-2);
	}

	.about__body p {
		margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
	}

	.about__body a {
		color: var(--pillar-strong);
		text-decoration: underline;
		text-underline-offset: 2px;
	}

	.about__disclaimer {
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: var(--size-sans-14);
		color: var(--neutral-38);
		border-left: 4px solid var(--pillar);
		padding-left: var(--space-3);
	}

	/* --- data status ------------------------------------------------------ */
	.status {
		max-width: var(--measure);
		margin-top: var(--space-8);
		border-top: 1px solid var(--section-border-primary);
		padding-top: var(--space-2);
	}

	.status__title {
		font-family: var(--font-headline);
		font-size: var(--size-headline-20);
		font-weight: 700;
		margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
	}

	.status__list {
		margin: 0;
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: var(--size-sans-15);
		line-height: var(--leading-sans);
	}

	.status__row {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: var(--space-1) var(--space-3);
		padding: var(--space-2) 0;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--straight-lines);
	}

	.status__row dt {
		flex: 0 0 11rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--neutral-38);
	}

	.status__row dd {
		margin: 0;
		flex: 1 1 12rem;
		min-width: 0;
		color: var(--neutral-7);
	}

	.status__note {
		padding-top: var(--space-4);
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: var(--size-sans-15);
	}

	.status__link {
		color: var(--pillar-strong);
		font-weight: 700;
		text-decoration: underline;
		text-underline-offset: 2px;
	}
</style>
